      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chronoranger_101/{size}/2112_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-06-18T03:54:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mackcrockett\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/53a042/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> mackcrockett:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I would argue that Akash works poorly with Rook City, she wants an environment with lots of targets like Final Wasteland, Block, or Enclave. Rook only has 3 targets, which means fewer free plays for her and fewer suprise Entombs. Her few copies of Disrupt the Field doesn't really offset that.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's true, but some of her cards play the environment which in turn could play the top card of the villain deck… Had this happen in a game a couple days ago… The ping pong effect was brutal. &nbsp;So while she works off of environment targets, even Rook City has advantages for her.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:20:04.103Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
